Runtime exceptions happen when your code tries an impossible action on real data.How to Catch and Handle Runtime ErrorsUnexpected runtime errors like server crashes or bad user inputs will happen. Building a safety net with a try...catch block helps you handle these surprises smoothly.1. Think of a  block as protective padding for your application. It acts as a shield to keep your code safe when unexpected errors happen. You tell the browser to  running a specific piece of code.If an error happens inside that block, your browser safely moves it to the catch zone. This keeps the rest of your webpage running without crashing.`javascript
